-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATA AND THIRD-PARTY MATERIALS — NOT COVERED BY THE MIT GRANT ABOVE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT License above applies to the source code and to documentation written
for this repository. It does not apply to, and does not sublicense, third-party
data, articles, or databases that the application displays or that are stored
beside the code.

1. openFDA product-label text is provided by the U.S. Food and Drug
   Administration under CC0 1.0. Do not rely on openFDA to make decisions
   regarding medical care.

2. NIH / NLM / RxNorm records are U.S. government public-domain data. NLM is
   not responsible for this product and does not endorse it. The verbatim NLM
   notice is shown in the application.

3. Europe PMC open-access articles remain under the Creative Commons license
   stated on each article (commonly CC BY 4.0 or CC BY-NC 4.0, not the public
   domain and not the MIT License). Display of an abstract or extract requires
   the creator names, the title, a link to that record's license, a link to the
   source, and a note when the text has been shortened. A blanket footer is not
   a substitute. The application renders those items on each literature card
   when Europe PMC returns them.

4. World Health Organization GLASS data, if a verbatim extract is ever added,
   remains under CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 IGO. That license's NonCommercial and
   ShareAlike terms are incompatible with the MIT License. Any such extract
   must stay in a separate file, keep WHO's mandatory attribution and
   non-endorsement notice, and must not be offered under MIT. The static
   resistance percentages shipped in this repository are developer-compiled
   educational illustrations. They are not a verbatim GLASS dataset, no
   surveillance year is stored with them, and they must not be cited as
   official WHO statistics. WHO does not endorse this project.

5. ECDC EARS-Net material may be reproduced only with a citation of the
   specific source report and year, and with a statement that adapted
   aggregations are the developer's responsibility, not ECDC's. This repository
   does not ship a verbatim EARS-Net table and does not store a report year.
   The EU/EEA percentages are the same kind of educational illustration and
   must not be cited as official EARS-Net rates. ECDC does not endorse this
   project.

6. Pathogen, syndrome, and drug-association indexes shipped with the
   application are maintained here as an educational compilation for this
   academic sandbox. The MIT License does not sublicense the Sanford Guide,
   UpToDate, Amboss, or any other commercial database, and these indexes are
   not offered as those works. A record that was taken from a protected
   database is not covered by the MIT grant. Where a record stores a public
   source URL, the application identifies that source. Individual facts are
   not, by themselves, a claim of copyright in those facts.

7. The MIT "AS IS" disclaimer is a software-license notice. It is not a waiver
   of liability for bodily injury, harm to health, or gross negligence, and it
   does not state that Directive (EU) 2024/2853 Article 2(2) displaces national
   fault-based tort law. Article 2(2) concerns the Directive's no-fault product
   liability for free and open-source software developed outside commercial
   activity. Article 2(4) preserves national fault-based rules.
